      "id": "T3",
      "name": "Symmetric-Matrix Transpose Identity and Exact Zero-Outcome Time-Reversal Duality",
      "statement": "For epsilon^rev = (epsilon_k, ..., epsilon_1) and sigma^rev = (sigma_(k-1), ..., sigma_1, sigma_k), complex symmetry of D_y and F_D implies <0_D | Psi_(epsilon, sigma)(y)> = <0_D | Psi_(epsilon^rev, sigma^rev)(y)> and P_(epsilon, sigma)(0 | y) = P_(epsilon^rev, sigma^rev)(0 | y) for all y in Z_q^D."
    }
  ],
